app std-orb-packages [
  version: "1.0.0",
  inbound: ["cli-packages"],
  env: ["PATH"],
  exec: [exe],
  sys: [identity],
  fs: { cwd: "**": [read, write, create, remove], "/**": [read], "~/.orb/**": [read, write, create, remove], "~/.orb": [create] },
  net: { "registry.npmjs.org:443": [tcp] },
  description: "std-orb-packages — the `orb list|add|update|remove [--global]` client of the npm registry (spec/cli/orb-packages.lolo; golden: orbital-cli packages.rs), bun-free. Packages live in <dir>/node_modules (dir = the working directory, or ~/.orb with --global) and the lockfile <dir>/<lockfile> holds { packages: [{ name, version, url, integrity }] }. Every command first reads the lockfile (absent = empty) and scans node_modules (scoped names included; the entry kind symlink is the workspace link), reading each package.json: a package is an orb package when it declares orbLanguage, orb, orbVocabulary or orbProgram.kind shell|desktop, and its kinds are those. list prints one row per orb package sorted by name (package 34, version 12, kinds 26, `ok`, ` (linked)`, ` [<prefix>/]`) or --json rows. remove refuses a behavior package whose prefix a .lolo or .orb file under the working directory still imports, deletes the package (a link is unlinked, never its target) and drops its lock entry. add parses name@exact-version (a range is refused ORB_PACKAGE_RANGE; a workspace-linked package is refused ORB_PACKAGE_LINKED) or a direct tarball URL (refused: it carries no integrity), and resolves name@version through GET <registry>/<name>/<version> (the npm version manifest: dist.tarball and dist.integrity). update reads the npm packument GET <registry>/<name> of every non-linked orb package and of every missing baseline package (an upgrade from nothing), and moves each to the newest stable, non-deprecated version above the installed one whose language is compatible: the running orb answers `orb --version` as `orb X.Y.Z (language R)` (any other form is refused) and keeps R; @almadar/core resolves first, and its candidate is compatible when its orbLanguage.version satisfies R; every other package is compatible when its language range (orb.language, orbLanguage.language, orbVocabulary.language or orbProgram.language, the first present) is satisfied by the target core language, the orbLanguage.version of the core version this update installs, else of the installed core; a version with no language is skipped ORB_PACKAGE_NO_LANGUAGE (compatibility is declared by the version itself, so one that declares nothing is never assumed compatible). The release version of orb is never compared with a package range. The tarball is downloaded from the registry knob (RegistryHttp) or the sourceOrigin knob (SourceHttp, one client per origin; any other host is refused ORB_PACKAGE_SOURCE), and its sha512 digest must equal the registry dist.integrity (sha512- plus base64, hash/sha): a different digest is refused `integrity-mismatch`, an unhashable one `integrity-unavailable`, and nothing is written or recorded. A verified tarball is gunzipped (maxUnpackedBytes) and read as a ustar archive (maxEntries) by the kernel; a codec refusal is ORB_PACKAGE_ARCHIVE (<code>), an entry outside package/ ORB_PACKAGE_LAYOUT. The files are written into node_modules/.orb-staging/<name>@<version> (mode 755 for executables, else 644), the old node_modules/<name> is renamed to node_modules/.orb-staging/<name>@<version>.old, the staging directory is renamed into place and only then is the backup removed (a failed rename into place renames the backup back and refuses the package ORB_PACKAGE_INSTALL, saying the previous version was restored; a failed restore names where the backup is kept; a leftover backup from an earlier crashed swap is never overwritten, it refuses the package); only then is the package's lock entry replaced and the lockfile written last. Every version may carry a top-level orbRelease block { severity security|critical|normal, advisory (one line), fixes (a semver range of the earlier versions it fixes) } in its registry manifest; no block is normal, and any other severity word is read as normal. update names, after the list rows, one `<severity> update: <name> <from> → <to>: <advisory>` line for each applied version whose own severity is security or critical. `orb update --urgent` (update only; with any other command it is refused with the usage line) installs only urgent updates: a package is urgent when some stable, non-deprecated version newer than the installed one is security or critical, declares a fixes range, the installed version satisfies that range (std-semver) and the version passes the language check above; the newest such version is installed through the same integrity check, staging swap and lockfile write, a baseline package that is not installed is never urgent, and stdout carries only the applied `<severity> update:` lines. An urgent version that fails the language check (ORB_PACKAGE_INCOMPATIBLE or ORB_PACKAGE_NO_LANGUAGE), whose fixes range std-semver refuses (ORB_PACKAGE_RELEASE), or that fails its download, integrity or install, is not applied: the installed version stays, the call answers 500, and stderr names the refusals and each confirmed-urgent advisory (a failed install leaves the old package in place, never half-installed). `orb update --global` also keeps this host's orb binary package (the orbPlatforms knob, matched on os/uname sysname and machine: @almadar/orb-darwin-arm64, -darwin-x64, -linux-x64, -linux-arm64, -windows-x64) installed like a baseline package, in the registry knob, with its own compatibility rule: it has no language range, so its newest stable, non-deprecated version is taken whose package.json declares orbReads, a range the target core language satisfies (a version without orbReads is skipped ORB_PACKAGE_NO_LANGUAGE; its orb and orbProgram blocks are not read); a package that declares orbReads is listed with kind `orb`; --urgent never installs it from nothing. A host that matches no entry, or whose os/uname fails (the Windows host does not implement it), prints one ORB_PACKAGE_PLATFORM line on stderr and no orb package is considered. A package whose package.json declares orbProgram also installs each of its optionalDependencies at its exact version whose registry manifest os and cpu include this host's (the os and cpu of the orbPlatforms entry os/uname matched, the npm platform rule; every add and update asks os/uname); a host os/uname cannot place installs none of them. Every file the package.json bin map names is written executable. Not yet ported: the kind-loads-for-this-orb problem column, the behaviors count, the update-check record and the engines subcommands; add does not remove a package that declares no orb kind."
]
uses Spec from "almadar-std/orb-packages"
uses Http from "std/behaviors/std-http-client"
type HttpHeader = { name : string!, value : string! }
type OrbCommandArgs = { argv : [string]!, cwd : string! }
type ArgFlag = { name : string!, aliases : [string]!, takesValue : boolean!, repeatable : boolean! }
type PackageKind = "language" | "behaviors" | "language pack" | "shell" | "desktop" | "orb"
type PackageRow = { package : string!, kinds : [PackageKind]!, version : string!, path : string!, link : boolean!, prefix : string?, behaviors : number?, problem : string? }
type LockEntry = { name : string!, version : string!, url : string!, integrity : string! }
type BaselineEntry = { name : string!, registry : string! }
type OrbPlatform = { sysname : string!, machine : string!, package : string!, os : string!, cpu : string! }
type LockFile = { packages : [LockEntry]! }
type PackageTarget = { name : string!, version : string!, url : string!, integrity : string!, severity : string?, advisory : string?, installedVersion : string?, platform : boolean? }
type Marker = { x : string? }
type LanguageBlock = { version : string? }
type OrbPackagesBlock = { prefix : string? }
type ProgramBlock = { kind : string?, name : string? }
type OrbPackagesManifest = { name : string?, version : string?, orbLanguage : LanguageBlock?, orb : OrbPackagesBlock?, orbVocabulary : Marker?, orbProgram : ProgramBlock?, orbReads : string?, optionalDependencies : Map string string?, bin : Map string string? }
type NpmDist = { tarball : string!, integrity : string? }
type NpmLanguage = { language : string?, version : string? }
type NpmRelease = { severity : string?, advisory : string?, fixes : string? }
type NpmManifest = { version : string!, deprecated : string?, dist : NpmDist?, orb : NpmLanguage?, orbLanguage : NpmLanguage?, orbVocabulary : NpmLanguage?, orbProgram : NpmLanguage?, orbRelease : NpmRelease?, orbReads : string?, os : [string]?, cpu : [string]? }
type Packument = { name : string!, versions : Map string NpmManifest! }
type Candidate = { version : string!, key : number!, language : string!, provides : string!, url : string!, integrity : string!, severity : string?, advisory : string?, fixes : string? }
type Subject = { package : string!, version : string!, missing : boolean! }
type TarEntry = { path : string!, data : bytes!, executable : boolean! }
type GzResult = { ok : boolean!, data : bytes, crc : number, code : string }
type TarResult = { ok : boolean!, entries : [TarEntry], code : string }
type Scanned = { name : string!, kind : string! }
type WalkOrb = { prefix : string?, registry : string?, source : string?, vectors : string?, language : string? }
type WalkManifest = { name : string?, version : string?, orb : WalkOrb? }
type LockedFile = { sha256 : string!, bytes : number!, url : string! }
type LockDoc = { version : number!, files : Map string LockedFile }
type WalkPkg = { name : string!, dir : string! }
type WalkRow = { name : string!, version : string!, root : string!, prefix : string!, registry : string?, source : string?, vectors : string?, language : string!, lock : LockDoc? }

orbital OrbPackagesOrbital {
  uses Args from "std/behaviors/std-args"
  uses Semver from "std/behaviors/std-semver"

  entity PackageCall [runtime] {
    id : string!
    status : number = 0
    lock : [LockEntry] = []
    cmd : string = ""
    args : [string] = []
    json : boolean = false
    global : boolean = false
    cwd : string = ""
    dir : string = ""
    lockDirty : boolean = false
    pkgs : [Scanned] = []
    scopes : [string] = []
    cursor : number = 0
    rows : [PackageRow] = []
    targets : [PackageTarget] = []
    refused : [string] = []
    out : [string] = []
    err : string = ""
    globs : [string] = []
    gcursor : number = 0
    paths : [string] = []
    hits : [string] = []
    tarballSize : number = 0
    digest : string = ""
    tarball : bytes = ""
    gz : GzResult?
    tar : TarResult?
    files : [TarEntry] = []
    ei : number = 0
    stage : string = ""
    installed : boolean = false
    done : [string] = []
    subjects : [Subject] = []
    pack : Packument?
    mf : NpmManifest?
    ancestors : boolean = false
    rungs : [string] = []
    wr : number = 0
    wcur : [WalkPkg] = []
    wpkgs : [WalkPkg] = []
    wc : number = 0
    wrows : [WalkRow] = []
    wpend : WalkRow = { name: "", version: "", root: "", prefix: "", language: "" }
    wpath : string = ""
    reads : string = ""
    coreLang : string = ""
    pid : number = 0
    reply : string = ""
    cands : [Candidate] = []
    ci : number = 0
    curKey : number = 0
    skipped : [string] = []
    urgent : boolean = false
    applied : [string] = []
    advisories : [string] = []
    hadOld : boolean = false
    orbPackage : string = ""
    unamed : boolean = false
    platformNote : string = ""
    hostOs : string = ""
    hostCpu : string = ""
    placeError : string = ""
  }

  trait RegistryHttp = Http.traits.HttpClient {
    config {
      host: "registry.npmjs.org"
      port: 443
      tls: true
      serverName: "registry.npmjs.org"
    }
    listens {
      OrbPackages.PK_GET -> HTTP_SEND
    }
  }

  trait SourceHttp = Http.traits.HttpClient {
    config {
      host: "registry.npmjs.org"
      port: 443
      tls: true
      serverName: "registry.npmjs.org"
    }
    listens {
      OrbPackages.PK_SRC_GET -> HTTP_SEND
    }
  }

  trait Versions = Semver.traits.Semver {
    listens {
      OrbPackages.PKG_SEMVER -> SEMVER_SATISFIES
    }
  }

  trait ArgsCli = Args.traits.ArgsParser {
    listens {
      OrbPackages.PKG_ARGS_PARSE -> ARGS_PARSE
    }
  }

  trait OrbPackages -> PackageCall [optimistic] {
    initial: ready

    state ready {
      INIT -> ready
      PACKAGES_CALLED -> parsing when (= (json/parse @payload.rawBody OrbCommandArgs) null)
        (emit PKG_ARGS_UNREAD { })
      PACKAGES_CALLED -> parsing when (!= (json/parse @payload.rawBody OrbCommandArgs) null)
        (set @entity.cwd (object/get (json/parse @payload.rawBody OrbCommandArgs) "cwd"))
        (let ((argv (object/get (json/parse @payload.rawBody OrbCommandArgs) "argv"))) (if (= @argv null) (emit PKG_ARGS_UNREAD { }) (emit PKG_ARGS_PARSE { stage: "packages" argv: @argv flags: [{ name: "json" aliases: [] takesValue: false repeatable: false }, { name: "global" aliases: [] takesValue: false repeatable: false }, { name: "ancestors" aliases: [] takesValue: false repeatable: false }, { name: "urgent" aliases: [] takesValue: false repeatable: false }] })))
    }

    state parsing {
      INIT -> parsing
      PKG_ARGS_UNREAD -> ready
        (emit PACKAGES_ANSWERED { status: 500, body: "", stderr: "Error: the call's arguments could not be read" })
      PKG_ARGS_DONE -> ready when (or (> (array/len @payload.errors) 0) (= (array/len @payload.positionals) 0) (not (array/includes ["list", "add", "update", "remove"] (array/first @payload.positionals))) (and (object/has @payload.flags "urgent") (!= (array/first @payload.positionals) "update")))
        (emit PACKAGES_ANSWERED { status: 400, body: "usage: orb list|add|update|remove [--json] [--global] [--urgent, update only] [<package>…]", stderr: "" })
      PKG_ARGS_DONE -> locating when (and (= (array/len @payload.errors) 0) (> (array/len @payload.positionals) 0) (array/includes ["list", "add", "update", "remove"] (array/first @payload.positionals)) (not (and (object/has @payload.flags "urgent") (!= (array/first @payload.positionals) "update"))))
        (set @entity.cmd (default (array/first @payload.positionals) ""))
        (set @entity.args (array/drop @payload.positionals 1))
        (set @entity.json (object/has @payload.flags "json"))
        (set @entity.global (object/has @payload.flags "global"))
        (set @entity.ancestors (object/has @payload.flags "ancestors"))
        (set @entity.urgent (object/has @payload.flags "urgent"))
        (set @entity.applied [])
        (set @entity.advisories [])
        (set @entity.orbPackage "")
        (set @entity.unamed false)
        (set @entity.platformNote "")
        (set @entity.hostOs "")
        (set @entity.hostCpu "")
        (set @entity.lock [])
        (set @entity.pkgs [])
        (set @entity.rows [])
        (set @entity.targets [])
        (set @entity.refused [])
        (set @entity.out [])
        (set @entity.lockDirty false)
        (set @entity.installed false)
        (set @entity.done [])
        (emit PKG_DIR { })
    }

    state locating {
      INIT -> locating
      PKG_DIR -> locking when @entity.global
        (set @entity.dir "~/.orb")
        (os/read-file (str/concat "~/.orb/" @config.lockfile) { key: "lock" emit: { success: PKG_LOCK_READ, failure: PKG_LOCK_ABSENT } })
      PKG_DIR -> locking when (not @entity.global)
        (set @entity.dir @entity.cwd)
        (os/read-file { anchor: "cwd" path: @config.lockfile } { key: "lock" emit: { success: PKG_LOCK_READ, failure: PKG_LOCK_ABSENT } })
    }

    state locking {
      INIT -> locking
      PKG_LOCK_READ -> scanning when (!= (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") LockFile) null)
        (set @entity.lock (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") LockFile) "packages"))
        (emit PKG_LIST_ROOT { })
      PKG_LOCK_READ -> ready when (= (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") LockFile) null)
        (emit PACKAGES_ANSWERED { status: 500, body: "", stderr: (str/concat @entity.dir "/" @config.lockfile ": not a valid lockfile (expected { packages: [{ name, version, url, integrity }] })") })
      PKG_LOCK_ABSENT -> scanning when (= @payload.kind "not-found")
        (emit PKG_LIST_ROOT { })
      PKG_LOCK_ABSENT -> ready when (!= @payload.kind "not-found")
        (emit PACKAGES_ANSWERED { status: 500, body: "", stderr: (str/concat @entity.dir "/" @config.lockfile ": " (default @payload.error "")) })
    }

    state scanning {
      INIT -> scanning
      PKG_LIST_ROOT -> scanning when @entity.global
        (os/list-dir "~/.orb/node_modules" { key: "root" emit: { success: PKG_ROOT, failure: PKG_ROOT_ABSENT } })
      PKG_LIST_ROOT -> scanning when (not @entity.global)
        (os/list-dir { anchor: "cwd" path: "node_modules" } { key: "root" emit: { success: PKG_ROOT, failure: PKG_ROOT_ABSENT } })
      PKG_ROOT -> scanning
        (set @entity.pkgs (array/map (array/filter @payload.entries (fn e (and (not (str/startsWith (object/get @e "name") ".")) (= (str/replace-pattern (object/get @e "name") "^\\x40" "") (object/get @e "name")) (array/includes ["dir", "symlink"] (object/get @e "kind"))))) (fn e { name: (object/get @e "name"), kind: (object/get @e "kind") })))
        (set @entity.scopes (array/map (array/filter @payload.entries (fn e (!= (str/replace-pattern (object/get @e "name") "^\\x40" "") (object/get @e "name")))) (fn e (object/get @e "name"))))
        (emit PKG_SCOPE { })
      PKG_ROOT_ABSENT -> scanning when (= @payload.kind "not-found")
        (set @entity.pkgs [])
        (set @entity.scopes [])
        (emit PKG_SCOPE { })
      PKG_ROOT_ABSENT -> ready when (!= @payload.kind "not-found")
        (emit PACKAGES_ANSWERED { status: 500, body: "", stderr: (str/concat @entity.dir "/node_modules: " (default @payload.error "")) })
      PKG_SCOPE -> scanning when (and (> (array/len @entity.scopes) 0) @entity.global)
        (os/list-dir (str/concat "~/.orb/node_modules/" (default (array/first @entity.scopes) "")) { key: "scope" emit: { success: PKG_SCOPED, failure: PKG_SCOPE_FAILED } })
      PKG_SCOPE -> scanning when (and (> (array/len @entity.scopes) 0) (not @entity.global))
        (os/list-dir { anchor: "cwd" path: (str/concat "node_modules/" (default (array/first @entity.scopes) "")) } { key: "scope" emit: { success: PKG_SCOPED, failure: PKG_SCOPE_FAILED } })
      PKG_SCOPE -> reading when (= (array/len @entity.scopes) 0)
        (set @entity.cursor 0)
        (set @entity.rows [])
        (emit PKG_READ { })
      PKG_SCOPED -> scanning
        (set @entity.pkgs (array/concat @entity.pkgs (array/map (array/filter @payload.entries (fn e (array/includes ["dir", "symlink"] (object/get @e "kind")))) (fn e { name: (str/concat (default (array/first @entity.scopes) "") "/" (object/get @e "name")), kind: (object/get @e "kind") }))))
        (set @entity.scopes (array/drop @entity.scopes 1))
        (emit PKG_SCOPE { })
      PKG_SCOPE_FAILED -> scanning
        (set @entity.scopes (array/drop @entity.scopes 1))
        (emit PKG_SCOPE { })
    }

    state reading {
      INIT -> reading
      PKG_READ -> reading when (and (< @entity.cursor (array/len @entity.pkgs)) @entity.global)
        (os/read-file (str/concat "~/.orb/node_modules/" (object/get (default (if (>= @entity.cursor 0) (array/nth @entity.pkgs @entity.cursor) null) { name: "", kind: "" }) "name") "/package.json") { key: "manifest" emit: { success: PKG_MANIFEST, failure: PKG_MANIFEST_FAILED } })
      PKG_READ -> reading when (and (< @entity.cursor (array/len @entity.pkgs)) (not @entity.global))
        (os/read-file { anchor: "cwd" path: (str/concat "node_modules/" (object/get (default (if (>= @entity.cursor 0) (array/nth @entity.pkgs @entity.cursor) null) { name: "", kind: "" }) "name") "/package.json") } { key: "manifest" emit: { success: PKG_MANIFEST, failure: PKG_MANIFEST_FAILED } })
      PKG_READ -> dispatching when (>= @entity.cursor (array/len @entity.pkgs))
        (set @entity.rows (array/sort @entity.rows "package" "asc"))
        (emit PKG_DISPATCH { })
      PKG_MANIFEST -> reading when (or (= (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) null) (and (= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbLanguage") null) (= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orb") null) (= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbVocabulary") null) (= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbReads") null) (not (array/includes ["shell", "desktop"] (default (object/get (default (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbProgram") { }) "kind") "")))))
        (set @entity.cursor (+ @entity.cursor 1))
        (emit PKG_READ { })
      PKG_MANIFEST -> reading when (and (!= (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) null) (or (!= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbLanguage") null) (!= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orb") null) (!= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbVocabulary") null) (!= (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbReads") null) (array/includes ["shell", "desktop"] (default (object/get (default (object/get (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest) "orbProgram") { }) "kind") ""))))
        (set @entity.rows (array/append @entity.rows (let ((m (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest)) (p (default (if (>= @entity.cursor 0) (array/nth @entity.pkgs @entity.cursor) null) { name: "", kind: "" }))) (let ((row { package: (object/get @p "name"), kinds: (array/concat (if (!= (object/get @m "orbLanguage") null) ["language"] []) (if (!= (object/get @m "orb") null) ["behaviors"] []) (if (!= (object/get @m "orbVocabulary") null) ["language pack"] []) (if (= (default (object/get (default (object/get @m "orbProgram") { }) "kind") "") "shell") ["shell"] []) (if (= (default (object/get (default (object/get @m "orbProgram") { }) "kind") "") "desktop") ["desktop"] []) (if (!= (object/get @m "orbReads") null) ["orb"] [])), version: (default (object/get @m "version") ""), path: (str/concat @entity.dir "/node_modules/" (object/get @p "name")), link: (= (object/get @p "kind") "symlink") })) (if (and (!= (object/get @m "orb") null) (!= (object/get (object/get @m "orb") "prefix") null)) (object/merge @row { prefix: (object/get (object/get @m "orb") "prefix") }) @row)))))
        (set @entity.coreLang (let ((m (json/parse (default (bytes/to-string @payload.data) "") OrbPackagesManifest))) (if (and (= (object/get (default (if (>= @entity.cursor 0) (array/nth @entity.pkgs @entity.cursor) null) { name: "", kind: "" }) "name") @config.corePackage) (!= (object/get @m "orbLanguage") null)) (default (object/get (object/get @m "orbLanguage") "version") @entity.coreLang) @entity.coreLang)))
        (set @entity.cursor (+ @entity.cursor 1))
        (emit PKG_READ { })
      PKG_MANIFEST_FAILED -> reading
        (set @entity.cursor (+ @entity.cursor 1))
        (emit PKG_READ { })
    }

    state dispatching {
      INIT -> dispatching
      PKG_DISPATCH -> listing when (and (= @entity.cmd "list") (not @entity.ancestors))
        (emit PKG_LIST { })
      PKG_DISPATCH -> walking when (and (= @entity.cmd "list") @entity.ancestors)
        (emit PKG_W_START { })
      PKG_DISPATCH -> ready when (and @entity.installed (= @entity.cmd "update"))
        (emit PACKAGES_ANSWERED { status: (if (and @entity.urgent (> (array/len @entity.skipped) 0)) 500 200), body: (if @entity.urgent (str/join @entity.applied "\n") (str/concat (str/join (array/map @entity.rows (fn r (str/concat (str/padEnd (object/get @r "package") 34 " ") " " (str/padEnd (object/get @r "version") 12 " ") " " (str/padEnd (str/join (object/get @r "kinds") ", ") 26 " ") " ok" (if (object/get @r "link") " (linked)" "")))) "\n") (if (> (array/len @entity.applied) 0) (str/concat "\n" (str/join @entity.applied "\n")) ""))), stderr: (if (and @entity.urgent (> (array/len @entity.skipped) 0)) (str/concat "orb update --urgent: an urgent update was not applied and the vulnerable version stays installed:\n  " (str/join @entity.skipped "\n  ") (if (> (array/len @entity.advisories) 0) (str/concat "\n  advisory: " (str/join @entity.advisories "\n  advisory: ")) "")) (str/join @entity.skipped "\n")) })
      PKG_DISPATCH -> ready when (and @entity.installed (= @entity.cmd "add"))
        (emit PACKAGES_ANSWERED { status: 200, body: (str/join (array/map @entity.done (fn n (let ((hit (array/filter @entity.rows (fn x (= (object/get @x "package") @n))))) (if (= (array/len @hit) 0) (str/concat "added " @n " (not an orb package: its package.json declares none of orbLanguage, orb, orbVocabulary, orbProgram)") (let ((r (default (array/first @hit) { package: "", kinds: [], version: "", path: "", link: false }))) (str/concat "added " @n (str/slice "a@b" 1 2) (object/get @r "version") " (" (str/join (object/get @r "kinds") ", ") ")")))))) "\n"), stderr: "" })
      PKG_DISPATCH -> removing when (= @entity.cmd "remove")
        (set @entity.cursor 0)
        (emit PKG_RM_NEXT { })
      PKG_DISPATCH -> ready when (and (not @entity.installed) (= @entity.cmd "add") (= (array/len @entity.args) 0))
